for s in steps:walk+=f'<section class="step workflow-step" id="workflow-step-{s["number"]:02}"><span class="number">{s["number"]:02}</span><h3>{s["number"]}. {s["title"]}</h3><p>{escape(s["explanation"])}</p><p class="source">Source: {s["source"]} · lines {s["firstLine"]}–{s["lastLine"]} · selected source; surrounding code omitted</p>'+snippet(s['code'])+'</section>'
document('/architecture.html','Architecture and <em>UML workflow.</em>','Every workflow step includes its corresponding coloured code excerpt.','<p class="note">The diagram groups alternative experiments: bounded direct agents, native limit cases and Workflow scripts. Numbered steps explain real source paths rather than implying every limit is reached in one run.</p><a class="button" href="/architecture.svg" download>Download UML SVG</a><div class="diagram"><img src="/architecture.svg" alt="Thirteen source-linked session workflow steps"></div>'+walk)

reference=[('Version and defaults', 'The lesson documents default depth 3, Agent concurrency 20 and no spend cap. This app pins the SDK and sets every cap explicitly. It uses three files rather than spending tokens on hundreds of workers; the same list/loop pattern illustrates larger runs.'), ('Depth versus a refusal', 'At depth 1 a child may not receive Agent at all and can perform its own permitted work. Depth2 demonstrates a real grandchild. Do not claim an error string must appear when the capability was removed before a call.'), ('Concurrency and incomplete work', 'The cap-one experiment asks for three background launches together. Native errors identify refused spawns. Reports must distinguish the admitted service from files that were never audited; do not infer complete coverage from a parent success result.'), ('Spend estimate and expected SDK exception', 'Budget mode is intentionally tiny. It retains error_max_budget_usd and the following SDK exception as expected evidence. An in-flight request can exceed the estimate before enforcement; maxBudgetUsd is not an exact billing guarantee. Do not blindly sum cumulative result frames.'), ('Opus 5 prompts and caps', 'The two Opus scenarios use an available Opus 5 model with either a custom instruction or claude_code preset plus an explicit user task. The model-specific delegation instruction steers behavior; depth/concurrency/spend controls remain necessary and explicit.'), ('Native Workflow evidence', 'The actual Workflow tool launches the reviewed script. Native lifecycle hooks observe child starts and stops, PreToolUse hooks observe real service reads, and task_notification reports workflow completion. Workflow child messages are not all forwarded as assistant events; do not mistake an empty direct-Agent catalog for no workflow work.'), ('Two concurrency mechanisms', 'CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONCURRENT_SUBAGENTS applies to direct Agent spawning. Workflow has its own CLAUDE_CODE_WORKFLOW_MAX_CONCURRENT_AGENTS resource setting. Fan-out uses two workflow slots; the serial script awaits each task and uses one. Inspect native lifecycle timing without promising a speedup.'), ('Script execution context', 'workflows/audit-parallel.js and audit-serial.js run inside the native Workflow runtime, which supplies agent, pipeline, phase and top-level return semantics. They are not standalone Node modules. The host reads only those packaged scripts and supplies one fixed script to the tool; students never need to paste arbitrary code.'), ('Primary documentation', 'See https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/subagents and https://code.claude.com/docs/en/workflows for native caps, Workflow execution and version-dependent behavior.')]
document('/walkthrough.html','How the app <em>was built.</em>','Every architecture step has source-linked coloured code.',cards(reference)+walk)
readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 45 · Scaling multi-agent workflows\n\nFive linked student pages, large text, actual SDK experiments and coloured code in all thirteen UML steps.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in learn)
readme+='\n## Configure and run\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/luiscoco/Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson45-app.git\ncd .\\Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson45-app\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start\n```\n\nFrom presentations use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson45-scaling-workflows`. Open http://127.0.0.1:3145 and keep the terminal running. Node.js 24+, API credit and model access are required. Windows may require Git Bash.\n\n## Create your .env file\n\nPreserve an existing file. Enter your own model key, then restart. Existing shell values take precedence.\n\n```dotenv\n'+env+'\n```\n\nNo GitHub token or Managed Agents IDs are required. Secrets, dependencies and teaching media stay outside Git.\n\n## Run the experiments\n\n'
for title,explanation,code in runsteps[3:]:readme+=f'### {title}\n\n{explanation}\n\n```powershell\n{code}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## How the app was built\n\n'
for step in steps:readme+=f'### {step["number"]}. {step["title"]}\n\n{step["explanation"]}\n\nSource: `{step["source"]}`, selected lines {step["firstLine"]}–{step["lastLine"]}. Surrounding code omitted.\n\n```typescript\n{step["code"]}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Reference topics and limits\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in reference)+'\n## References\n\n- [Official SDK subagents documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/subagents)\n- [TypeScript SDK reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/typescript)\n\nRegenerate student pages with `python scripts/build-pages.py`. Run `npm test` for specialist definitions, bounded delegation, scoped tools, actual fixture behavior and startup checks.\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five Lesson 45 pages and thirteen source-linked UML steps.')

(PUBLIC/"style.css").write_text((PUBLIC/"style.css").read_text(encoding="utf-8")+'\n#conversation{max-height:540px;overflow:auto}.markdown-body{font-size:22px;line-height:1.6}.markdown-body article,#conversation article{padding:16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.json-view{max-height:380px}#result-history td{max-width:380px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.table{max-height:350px;overflow:auto}#branch-cards{grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,300px),1fr))}#branch-cards .branch-card{padding:20px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}#branch-cards .meta{font-size:20px}#session-picker{font-size:21px}#picker-panel .meta{margin-bottom:0}\n',encoding="utf-8")
